  "name": "Vocoder",
  "description": "Stereo spectral vocoder. Each speech channel is strongly compressed and filtered to 300 Hz–3 kHz before shaping its corresponding carrier channel. Route speech to speech and a harmonically rich carrier to sound. A stereo-linked output compressor controls syllable peaks. Set Output Compression Ratio from 1:1 to 10:1 (default 4:1). Dry Mixin adds the original stereo carrier before output compression, with logarithmic gain from 0.0001 (default) to 0.1.",
